{
  "name": "Cloud Office Print - PDF Operations with Google Drive",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Convert, watermark and compress\n\n**Before running:** set your credential on every Cloud Office Print, Google Drive and Google Sheets node, one by one. n8n does not copy credentials across imported nodes. Then pick your own files in the empty File and Document fields.\n\nTakes a Word file from Drive, converts it to PDF, stamps CONFIDENTIAL on every page, compresses it and uploads the result.\n\nThe Cloud Office Print node returns Base64 in `body`, so one node feeds the next with `{{ $json.body }}`. Convert to File is only needed once, at the end.\n\n### Setup\nUpload `docs/assets/samples/sample-document.docx` to your Drive, then select it below.\n\nThis workflow has **four** Cloud Office Print nodes across its two flows. Each one needs its credential set separately: Convert to PDF, Add CONFIDENTIAL watermark, Compress PDF, and Merge files into one PDF further down the canvas.",
        "height": 486,
        "width": 2220,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        0
      ],
      "id": "3f4e14c3-c751-4415-803f-283219257a19",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Pipeline overview"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        981
      ],
      "id": "8b6bcdbf-d821-4071-81fe-cb39125ee64e",
      "name": "When clicking 'Execute workflow'"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Trigger\n\nRuns on demand.\n\nA Google Drive Trigger watching a folder is a good replacement: every document dropped in gets processed.",
        "height": 425,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
